emscripten 5.0.1 (as installed by emsdk) — six hand-written heap indexings use a
SIGNED shift, which is wrong above 2 GiB under CAN_ADDRESS_2GB.

PROPOSAL, NOT APPLIED LOCALLY. picovoxel does not use these GL bindings; this
patch exists because we paid for the bug class in our own glue and found that
upstream has stragglers of the same shape. Ledger row U24.

The rule upstream already follows: emscripten's own codegen knows about this.
`getHeapOffset` (src/parseTools.mjs:399-410) emits `>>>` instead of `>>` when
CAN_ADDRESS_2GB is set, and CAN_ADDRESS_2GB is set automatically whenever
MAXIMUM_MEMORY > 2 GiB (tools/link.py:1680-1681). Every access written through
the macro is therefore correct.

The defect: six accesses in the WebGL libraries are written by hand and bypass
the macro, so they keep the signed shift under every setting. A pointer at or
past 2 GiB is >= 2**31; JS `>>` coerces to int32 first, so `p >> 2` goes
negative, and the resulting index reads the wrong element (or, for the
`subarray`/`set` family, silently clamps). The neighbouring
`glUniformMatrix4x3fv` in the very same file uses
`{{{ getHeapOffset('value', 'float') }}}` — the two idioms sit five lines apart.

  src/lib/libwebgl.js:3019,3028,3037,3046  glVertexAttrib{1,2,3,4}fv
  src/lib/libwebgl2.js:881,889             glVertexAttribI4{i,ui}v

The fix is `>>` -> `>>>` at those sites, which is a no-op below 2 GiB and
correct above it. (A stricter fix would route them through `getHeapOffset` for
MEMORY64 as well; these entry points are !MEMORY64-only paths today, so this
patch keeps the change to the minimum that removes the defect.)

Provenance: picovoxel spent a spike (bench/results/webgpu-v2/SK-0.10.md) rooting
a silent mesh corruption to exactly this class in our OWN hand-written glue —
`HEAPU32.subarray(pointer >> 2, ...)` on a 120 MB staging buffer that the
allocator happened to place above 2 GiB. `TypedArray.subarray` clamps a negative
start instead of throwing, so the read succeeded, returned a correctly-sized
window ~1.4 GiB away from the buffer, and every cheap invariant (element count,
byte count, volume) still passed. That part is our bug, not emscripten's; these
six lines are the part that is upstream's.

